WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.640
The Netflix roster of Marvel shows has already
shown that they're capable of drawing some

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.890
great moments from the comics and transferring
them to the screen.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.500
And with the Punisher, they're spoiled for
choice.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.620
With hundreds of comics and decades of stories
to draw from, all built around hard-hitting

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.900
ultra-violent action, there are plenty of
brutal moments that are begging to be recreated.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.099
There is, however, a problem unique to the
Punisher: a lot of his stories might just

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:25.289
be too intense to work on the show.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:27.250
And more are just intensely weird.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.700
And yes — they're actually weirder than
this:

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.220
Here are some Punisher comic book moments
that'll never make it to Netflix.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.230
Army of One

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.620
It goes without saying that any media project
involving Frank Castle is going to draw heavily

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.460
from Garth Ennis's eight years of writing
the character.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:54.400
The Netflix shows have already started, with
an adaptation of the issue where the Punisher

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.480
ties Daredevil up to witness a rooftop execution.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.520
But over the course of those eight years,
Ennis got into some pretty extreme stories.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.130
In "Army of One," the Punisher took on an
entire island full of killer mercenaries,

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:11.160
including his long-time nemesis, the Russian,
who we've seen in the 2004 Punisher movie:

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.040
So why's the story so problematic?

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:26.460
Well, it's Frank's solution that causes trouble:
going for the nuclear option — literally.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.090
The story ends with a mushroom cloud when
the Punisher drops an atomic bomb onto the

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:35.100
island and its mercenary inhabitants, wiping
them all from the face of the Earth.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.100
Crackdown

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.840
Considering that the shows have already introduced
Luke Cage, it's easy to imagine that they

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.609
might want to tie the Punisher into the MCU
by re-creating one of their classic team-ups.

00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:49.110
Unfortunately, their most notable meeting
involves Frank Castle changing his skin color

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:53.440
and pretending to be a black man for three
issues until he eventually fades back to his

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.079
usual Caucasian complexion.

00:01:55.079 --> 00:02:00.159
In "Crackdown," Frank is sent to jail and
gets his face carved up by the bad guy Jigsaw.

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:04.159
After that, we see Frank's face get repaired
by a surgeon, whose experimental technique

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:07.790
involved pumping the Punisher full of the
skin pigment melanin.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:12.400
The result was a dark-skinned, and ridiculously
inappropriate Punisher, who teams up with

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.270
Luke Cage in Chicago to bring down a ring
of crack dealers — and an army of ninjas.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:22.020
Needless to say, after three issues, this
whole thing was never mentioned again.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.060
FrankenCastle

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:27.690
Believe it or not, the tale of the temporarily
black Frank Castle isn't actually the weirdest

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:31.940
Punisher story — and neither is the time
he became an angel who killed demons with

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.220
magical ghost guns.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.700
No, that honor goes to when he spent a year
as a Frankenstein.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.580
In 2009, the notorious supervillain Norman
Osborn — better known to Spider-Man fans

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.160
as the Green Goblin — was put in charge
of national security.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:49.660
An unrepentant murderer in a position of power
made for a tempting target, and Frank set

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.700
his sights on taking Osborn down.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.700
The problem?

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.400
Frank's just a guy with a lot of guns — and
Osborn had his own team of Dark Avengers protecting

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.400
him.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.200
Daken, the son of Wolverine, ended up chopping
the Punisher to pieces and throwing his body

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:07.200
into a sewer… where it was found and stitched
back together by Morbius the Living Vampire,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.350
who resurrected him to protect a secret city
of monsters underneath Manhattan.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:16.090
Chances are good that won't happen on TV anytime
soon: even if Jon Bernthal would look pretty

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.390
great as a Frankenstein.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.990
Punisher kills Nick Fury

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:24.310
If they really wanted to tie Bernthal's version
of the Punisher to the larger Marvel Cinematic

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:28.460
Universe, they could always go with one of
Frank's other big encounters with the MCU's

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.900
most prominent characters.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.050
Like that time he murdered Nick Fury.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:37.520
In 1995, the Punisher was captured by renegade
S.H.I.E.L.D. agents and brainwashed into believing

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.460
that it was actually Fury who killed his family
— so he shot and killed him.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.180
After a manhunt involving the Avengers, he
was arrested and sentenced to death in the

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.480
electric chair.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.810
Because it's comics, neither death really
lasted long.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:53.470
It was later revealed that Tony Stark had
invented a special "Life Model Decoy" robot

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.770
that managed to fool everyone.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.050
And the Punisher?

00:03:56.050 --> 00:04:00.210
He was rescued from the electric chair by
a mafioso who wanted him to take over his

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.210
organization.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:06.390
He actually agreed, and briefly joined up
as the new head of an organized crime family.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.960
Frank's hydrophobia

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:12.870
In the pages of Punisher War Journal, we finally
discover the Punisher's a weakness: a crippling

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:17.389
fear of open water, dating back to a childhood
trauma — because what the Punisher really

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:19.810
needed was to have a more traumatic past.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:24.030
When Frank found himself tracking down a gang
of drug dealers to Hawaii, his fear almost

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.159
got him killed.

00:04:25.159 --> 00:04:29.139
Luckily, he was rescued from drowning by a
friendly dolphin and then conquered his fear

00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:33.330
with the help of a local kahuna who healed
his spirit with magic at the request of a

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.540
ninja master.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.080
No, really.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.720
Even if it's unlikely we'll ever see this
story make it to the screen, let's not kid

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:40.720
ourselves.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:41.720
It would be amazing.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:45.270
Who wouldn't want to see Frank Castle wearing
a bright Hawaiian shirt over his Punisher

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.789
outfit, or watch the Punisher ride a jet-ski?

00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:51.129
The cover blurb says it all: "You just rented
a jet-ski to the Punisher.

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:53.560
KISS THAT BABY GOODBYE!"

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.050
Punisher Meets Archie

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:59.409
If there's a hall of fame for bizarre comic
book crossovers, then The Punisher Meets Archie

00:04:59.409 --> 00:05:00.909
is a first-round pick.

00:05:00.909 --> 00:05:05.960
Originally published in 1994, it stands as
one of the weirdest of all time, even after

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:10.960
a decade of Archie meeting everyone from Barack
Obama and Sarah Palin, to the Predator, to

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.270
Sharknado.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.440
Yes, that Sharknado.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:21.439
But incredibly, this team-up is actually more
plausible than ever.

00:05:21.439 --> 00:05:25.479
On TV's Riverdale, a show with no shortage
of murders, the Archie gang's gone through

00:05:25.479 --> 00:05:26.479
a pretty dark re-imagining.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.240
So having Frank Castle roll up to lay down
some vigilante justice wouldn't seem strange

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.140
at all.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.300
Is it going to happen?

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:34.500
No.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.580
But if we don't at least get a cameo appearance
from Archie-actor K.J.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:41.120
Apa as a redheaded criminal on the run from
the Punisher, then what are we even doing

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.120
here?

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:43.920
Thanks for watching!

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.770
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.999
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love too!

